---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import HBand from '../components/HBand.astro';
import agentsImg from '../assets/doors/agents.jpg';
import '../styles/interior.css';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="For Real Estate Agents · Alliance Mutual Escrow"
  description="A closing partner for California agents: proactive status, one licensed officer per file, and clean timelines that protect your client relationship."
  bodyClass="page-interior"
  navVariant="solid"
  navMax={1080}
>
  <header class="hero">
    <div class="kick">For real estate agents</div>
    <h1>Your client. Your relationship. <i>Our paperwork.</i></h1>
    <p class="sub">
      You spent months earning that trust. Our job is to close on time, with no surprises, so your
      client remembers you chose well.
    </p>
  </header>

  <HBand image={agentsImg} tag="The long view" />

  <div class="wrap">
    <main>
      <h2>What working with us feels like</h2>
      <p>
        <b>One licensed officer owns the file</b> from open to close. You are never re-routed, never
        re-explaining, never chasing a call center. Status moves to you before you have to ask, so
        your client hears news from you first.
      </p>
      <p>
        We chase demands, disclosures, HOA documents, and payoffs early, because the quiet weeks in
        the middle of an escrow are where late closings are born. When something threatens the date,
        you hear it from us the same day, with the plan already attached.
      </p>

      <div class="quiet">
        <div class="qt">The quiet work, done early</div>
        <div class="qi"><svg viewBox="0 0 18 18"><path d="M3 9.5l4 4 8-9" /></svg><span>Payoff demands ordered at open, not at the deadline</span></div>
        <div class="qi"><svg viewBox="0 0 18 18"><path d="M3 9.5l4 4 8-9" /></svg><span>HOA documents chased before they can slow the file</span></div>
        <div class="qi"><svg viewBox="0 0 18 18"><path d="M3 9.5l4 4 8-9" /></svg><span>Disclosures and demands verified line by line</span></div>
        <div class="qi"><svg viewBox="0 0 18 18"><path d="M3 9.5l4 4 8-9" /></svg><span>Status to you before your client has to ask</span></div>
      </div>

      <h2>Opening an escrow</h2>
      <p>
        Send the purchase agreement and we take it from there: file opened, timeline set,
        introductions made to both sides with plain instructions for what happens next. Your buyers
        and sellers get a named officer and a direct line.
      </p>

      <h2>Frequently asked</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <div class="fq">
          <h3>Why does independent matter to my clients?</h3>
          <p>
            An independent escrow answers to the file, not to a brokerage or a bank that also has a
            side in the deal. Licensed by the DFPI, audited, and neutral by charter. It is an easy
            trust story to tell your clients.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="fq">
          <h3>How do you handle a rough file?</h3>
          <p>
            Early and out loud. Solar transfers, subordinations, seller payoffs that will not add up:
            we surface problems while there is still calendar left to fix them.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="fq">
          <h3>Do my clients pay more for this?</h3>
          <p>
            No. Our fees are published: $300 plus $2.15 per $1,000, each side, with flat add-ons
            listed in the open. No mystery line items for you to explain later.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </main>

    <aside class="aside">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="ch">What your clients get</div>
        <div class="fr"><span class="k">A named licensed officer</span><span class="v">DAY 1</span></div>
        <div class="fr"><span class="k">Direct line, no call center</span><span class="v">ALWAYS</span></div>
        <div class="fr"><span class="k">Wire verification by phone</span><span class="v">EVERY WIRE</span></div>
        <div class="fr"><span class="k">Status before you ask</span><span class="v">WEEKLY+</span></div>
        <div class="fr tot"><span class="k">Late-closing surprises</span><span class="v">NONE PLANNED</span></div>
        <div class="cn">The goal is boring closings, on the date, with your name looking good.</div>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>

  <section class="cta">
    <div class="cta-in">
      <h2>Open your next escrow <i>with us.</i></h2>
      <a class="btn" href="tel:7145446525">Talk to a licensed officer</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <p class="note">
    Sample page for design review. Copy is draft, written fresh; figures are from the published fee
    schedule. Third-party costs are estimates from providers you choose.
  </p>

  <script>
    import '../scripts/interior-motion';
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
